.TH DQL-EDITOR 1 "2026-08-08" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-editor \- export the embedded editor-support artifacts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql editor export-artifacts
.RB [ \-\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B dql
binary carries its own editor support: the authored tree-sitter
grammar, the highlight query files, and the compiled parser shared
library, embedded as a read-only database image. This command writes
those artifacts to disk in one layout serving two consumers:
.PP
.EX
DIR/parser/delightql.so        compiled parser
DIR/queries/delightql/*.scm    highlight queries
DIR/grammar/                   tree-sitter project sources
.EE
.PP
Point an editor's runtime path at
.I DIR
and it finds the parser and queries by convention.
.I DIR/grammar
is a complete tree-sitter project: the grammar sources suffice to
regenerate and recompile the parser on a platform other than the one
this binary was built for.
.PP
The embedded parser fits exactly one platform \(em the one the binary
was compiled for \(em and speaks one tree-sitter ABI version. The
closing output line names both, so a mismatch is visible before an
editor attempts to load the library.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR export-artifacts " [" \-\-dir " \fIDIR\fP]"
Write every artifact into
.I DIR
(default: the current directory). Directories are created as needed;
existing files are overwritten. Each written path is printed on its own
line, followed by the parser's platform target and tree-sitter ABI
version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " DIR"
Output directory for
.BR export-artifacts .
Defaults to the current directory.
.SH DATA ACCESS
The same artifacts are queryable in any session without touching disk:
.PP
.EX
mount!("delightql-bytes://editor", "e")(*)
e::(*)
e.parser_artifact(*) |> (target, abi_version)
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-query (1)
